  "title": "Executor attribution: a codex row id in tier is labelled as that codex executor, never claude:<id>",
  "spec": "Goal T-1403, wave 2, plan label E11 (part b).\n\nWhere 'claude:astra' comes from (2026-10-01):\n- `uv run orchestrator scorecard` shows rows claude:astra (13 merged / 59 failed), claude:luna, claude:sol,\n  claude:terra. Source: execute task files with executor None and tier '<codex id>' (orchestrator: 96 tasks\n  tier astra, 18 sol, 11 luna, 5 terra, executor None) go through orchestrator/scorecard.py:189-193 key_of():\n  entry.get('executor') or f\"claude:{entry['tier']}\".\n- Run rows: .orchestrator/runs/*.jsonl hold 110 rows with executor claude:astra/sol/luna/terra (roles memory and\n  env_policy, e.g. T-1399 memory rows 2026-09-30). They are written by orchestrator/bus.py:366 and 380-383\n  log_run(): provider defaults to 'claude' unless account == 'codex', then executor = task.executor or\n  (tier if provider == 'codex' else f\"claude:{tier}\").\n- executor.py:532 sets executor = tier = ex.id for codex claims, so tier holds codex row ids.\n- pool.executor_rows(cfg) (orchestrator/pool.py:145-153) lists configured rows with provider.\n\nChange:\n1. attribution.executor_label(executor, tier, cfg) -> str | None: executor when set; else if executor is a\n   'claude:<x>' string whose <x> is a codex row id, that id; else tier when tier is a configured row id with\n   provider 'codex' (pool.executor_rows(cfg)) ; else f\"claude:{tier}\" when tier; else None. Also normalise a stored\n   'claude:<codex id>' executor to '<codex id>'.\n2. scorecard.py key_of() (by='executor') uses it with pool config (import inside the function, fall back to the\n   current behaviour if config cannot load). by='tier' unchanged.\n3. bus.log_run(): executor default uses executor_label; when the resolved label is a codex row and the caller passed\n   neither provider nor account, provider becomes 'codex'.\n\nTests that assert the old behaviour (SPEC RULE): tests/test_scorecard.py::test_review_task_does_not_double_count_verdict\n(~429-435, tier sonnet -> claude:sonnet) and test_by_tier_regroups (~442-445) must pass unchanged;\ntests/test_bus.py rows near ~126 (explicit executor astra, account codex) and ~229-246 (account-based provider) must\npass unchanged. Run tests/test_scorecard.py, tests/test_bus.py and tests/test_attribution.py.\n\nDepends on E8 (bus.py, tests/test_bus.py).\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused tests in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate. Write tests as unittest.TestCase methods using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_scorecard.py::test_legacy_codex_tier_rows_keep_codex_label: passes: scorecard.build() over a task with executor None and tier 'astra' and a run row whose stored executor is 'claude:astra' counts both under 'astra' and creates no 'claude:astra' key, while tier 'sonnet' still maps to 'claude:sonnet'",
    "tests/test_bus.py::test_log_run_without_account_labels_codex_tier_as_codex: passes: bus.log_run(task=t) for a task with executor None and tier 'astra', with no account, writes executor 'astra' and provider 'codex'",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
